id: divine-attack
name: Divine Attack
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: true
requiresTarget: true
profile: any
usageLimit: 1/round
# A God Maneuver: open where an effect grants it, only in God Ki, paid in Divine Ki Points (maneuvers.mjs whyNotGod,
# spendManeuverCost). "The DKP Cost is equal to the KP Cost of your chosen Profile, after applying any reductions from
# effects, and is paid instead of it" - the Profile's price as it is worked out, in DKP. "This Attacking Maneuver has its
# Damage Category increased by 1 category" - the Maneuver's own shift, carried on the attack.
godManeuver: true
damageCategoryShift: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A God Maneuver: an attack as the Basic Attack, its Profile's KP Cost paid in Divine Ki Points, its Damage Category one
  higher.
text: >
  Divine Attack [1/Round]: You attack with divine might.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –DKP Cost: Variable
  –Effect: Make an Attacking Maneuver as if this was the Basic Attack Maneuver. The DKP Cost is equal to the KP Cost of
  your chosen Profile, after applying any reductions from effects, and is paid instead of it. This Attacking Maneuver has
  its Damage Category increased by 1 category.
